### Usuarios: alta, cambios, contraseña y bajas (modalidad JWT + RBAC: solo ADMIN)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api
@token = <access_token>
@id = 6

### create -> 201 (password guardada como hash)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "operario.bascula",
  "email": "operario.bascula@circularguajira.co",
  "password": "Bascula2026!"
}

### create: username repetido -> 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "email": "otro@circularguajira.co",
  "password": "Clave2026!"
}

### PUT: identidad completa (sin password ni status) -> 200
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/{{id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "operario.bascula",
  "email": "operario.bascula@circularguajira.co",
  "avatar": "https://circularguajira.co/avatars/bascula.png"
}

### PATCH: parcial -> 200; password/status aquí -> 400
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/{{id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "avatar": null
}

### cambio de contraseña: exige la actual -> 200 (400 si la actual no coincide)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/{{id}}/password
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "Bascula2026!",
  "newPassword": "Bascula2027!"
}

### deactivate (lógico): sus tokens dejan de valer de inmediato
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/{{id}}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### delete (físico)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/{{id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
